  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is positive (0.00–0.50) and model shows over-optimism (e.g., >10% above recent mean).",
    "Reduce forecast peaks by 5–10% after spikes, especially if sentiment is neutral or slightly positive (0.00–0.33).",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates >15% from 14-day moving average, adjust toward it with sentiment-weighted damping.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25 or below) and forecast is above recent range.",
    "For 30-day horizon, reduce forecast volatility if sentiment is stable (±0.00–0.25) to avoid overfitting to short-term noise."
  ]
}
